BypassAIGC Skill: LaTeX Academic Revision

Project inspiration and attribution
==================================

This project was inspired by the open-source project:

  BypassAIGC / AI 学术写作助手
  https://github.com/chi111i/BypassAIGC

The original project provides the broader application idea around academic
writing assistance, paper polishing, staged revision, and writing workflow
management.

This repository is an independent Codex / OpenAI Agents skill that adapts the
general idea into a LaTeX-first, auditable agent workflow. It focuses on prompt
engineering, LaTeX structure protection, revision packets, protected-token
checks, and safe academic prose revision.

This repository does not include the original project's frontend/backend
application code, database models, executable packaging logic, or management
dashboard implementation.

The original BypassAIGC project is licensed separately. At the time this notice
was written, its repository states CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Users who copy, adapt, or
redistribute material from the original project should follow the original
project's license terms.

This repository's own code and documentation are distributed under the MIT
License unless otherwise stated.

Additional source-review notes
==============================

In 2026, this project also reviewed and distilled high-level workflow ideas
from several open-source academic-writing, prompt-library, prompt-optimizer,
and style-diagnostic projects. The reviewed sources and license notes are
recorded in references/source-digests.md.

These sources were used as methodology references only: staged revision,
prompt organization, citation-oriented QA, style-pattern diagnostics, and
prompt evaluation loops. This repository does not vendor their application
code or reuse detector-evasion instructions.
